# The sites the "Chosen sites" switch sends through the Mac in Japan. The installer copies this file
# to ~/.config/macmini-vpn/sites the first time and never overwrites your copy. After an edit, apply
# it with the menu (switch "Chosen sites" off and on) or `mmvpn set sites` (plus any other routes
# you want); browsers and apps then fetch the new list at once.
#
# One entry per line; # starts a comment.
#   example.jp              the domain and every name under it (www.example.jp, cdn.example.jp)
#   *-video.cdn.example     a pattern with *, matched against the whole host name
# Every host of a listed site goes through the same exit, sign-in and video included, with no
# fallback. List the domains the video streams from too: they are often not the site's own domain.
# Your browser's developer tools (Network tab) show them.
#
# Shared CDNs such as akamaized.net carry many companies' traffic, so a pattern for one should name
# the service at a hyphen or label boundary (*-abematv.akamaized.net), never the whole CDN.

# ABEMA: pages, API, and video from Akamai
abema.tv
abema.io
*-abematv.akamaized.net
abematv.akamaized.net

# TVer
tver.jp

# radiko: pages, and audio from its own CDNs
radiko.jp
*-radiko.smartstream.ne.jp
radiko.smartstream.ne.jp
*.radiko-cf.com

# NHK: pages, and simulcast video
nhk.or.jp
nhk.jp
*.drdi.st.nhk

# Netflix: pages, sign-in, scripts (nflxext.com), images (nflxso.net, nflximg.net/.com) and video
# (Open Connect, nflxvideo.net)
netflix.com
netflix.net
nflxvideo.net
nflxso.net
nflximg.net
nflximg.com
nflxext.com
